Package: islasso
Type: Package
Title: The Induced Smoothed Lasso
Version: 1.7.0
Date: 2026-11-25
Authors@R: c(
    person("Gianluca", "Sottile", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "gianluca.sottile@unipa.it",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9347-7251")),
    person("Giovanna", "Cilluffo", role = "aut"),
    person("Vito M. R.", "Muggeo", role = "aut"))
Description: An implementation of the induced smoothing (IS) idea to lasso and
    elastic-net regularisation models, allowing estimation and inference
    (standard errors and Wald tests) on all the model coefficients. Any
    generalised linear model family can be used. The numerical core, written in C
    with 'BLAS' and 'LAPACK', solves the smoothed estimating equations by
    majorise-minimise or Newton iterations and switches to Woodbury identities when
    the covariates outnumber the observations. The method is described in
    Cilluffo et al. (2020) <doi:10.1177/0962280219842890> and in a tutorial
    <doi:10.13140/RG.2.2.16360.11521>.
